[h2]Fixed: armour now drops like armour, and no single weapon class runs away with a run[/h2]

[b]Two player reports, both real, both measured.[/b] The first: shields, chest plates and helmets almost never showed up. The second: one run produced four copies of the same legendary spear. The previous update proved a chest [i]could[/i] pay every weapon class; it never checked how [i]often[/i]. Measured on the build that shipped, a six chest boss run paid 58.5 legendary weapons against 12.4 armour pieces, helmets were 1.6 percent of everything that dropped, and spears alone took 24 percent when an even split across the eleven gear slots is 9.1 percent.

[list]
[*][b]Armour is on equal footing with weapons.[/b] Every armour row now fires at the weapon row's own rate, the legendary share inside each armour row went from roughly a tenth to about half, and a new armour master pays all five worn slots evenly. Armour pieces per six chest run go from 12.4 to 49.4, and the weapon to armour ratio from 4.73 to 1 down to 1.22 to 1.
[*][b]No class dominates any more.[/b] All eleven gear classes now land between 7.8 and 10.8 percent of a run, against an even split of 9.1 percent. The old spread ran from 1.6 percent to 24 percent. Spears drop from 24 percent to 9.8 percent; helmets rise from 1.6 percent to 8.7 percent.
[*][b]The four identical spears, specifically.[/b] The odds of some legendary spear landing four times in one run fall from 27 percent to 6.3 percent. One table that covered axes, maces and swords together had been carrying a single spear's weight, so each of those three classes got a third of a spear's chance; that is fixed, and the per chest theme biases were softened.
[*][b]Boss orb chests were the worst offenders and had been missed.[/b] The chests behind the red uber mystical orbs were paying 0.07 helmets per open against 0.98 weapons. They now pay about 1.2 of every worn slot. Boss hoards, the guard pair hoards and the blood cave mega chest all got the identical treatment.
[*][b]Nothing was taken away.[/b] Spawn count equations are untouched and total legendary gear per run actually rises, from about 71 to about 109. Across the whole database this update raised 603 values and lowered none, added 60 loot entries and removed none.
[*][b]A permanent gate so it cannot come back.[/b] The build now fails loudly if any loot surface skews toward one class, lets one item dominate, or starves a worn slot. It audits 42 surfaces and is checked against seven deliberately broken builds.
[/list]

[i]This update changes loot tables only. No stat, skill, monster, quest or map was touched. The uber orb weapon breadth, the portal page cap, the Epic and Legendary soul names, the Boar Snatcher orb, the Spartan Crypt entrance and the chest breadth work from the previous updates are all included.[/i]
